Marissa / Monica — we need an implementation plan that covers SDK install, endpoint migration path (Blue/Green), and operational guidance for retries and rate limits. Susan has provided traffic forecasts above.

Action items: 
- Marissa: create the "BrightCart integration runbook" with the following sections: env setup, SDK quickstart (Node + Python examples), CI/CD config for model pinning, and cutover checklist.
- Monica: own the MAP and schedule the kickoff (30–45 minutes). Please include SRE and security contacts.
- Jonas: provide sample code and allowlist matrix.

Sample code snippet (Node.js, quickstart):

const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, model: 'gpt-redwood-1' });

// embeddings sample
async function embed(text) {
  const res = await client.embeddings.create({ input: text });
  return res.data[0].embedding;
}

// generation with retry helper
async function generateWithRetry(prompt) {
  let attempt = 0;
  const maxAttempts = 5;
  while (attempt < maxAttempts) {
    try {
      return await client.generate({ prompt, max_tokens: 256, timeout: 30000 });
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429 || err.status === 503) {
        const backoff = Math.min(10000, 200 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff + Math.floor(Math.random() * 200)));
        attempt++;
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('Max retries exceeded');
}

Endpoint migration pattern (recommended):
- Phase A (pre-prod): point non-critical traffic to Redwood sandbox endpoints.
- Phase B (canary): route 1–5% production traffic with feature flags; monitor latency, error-rate, token costs.
- Phase C (gradual ramp): double traffic every 12–24 hours while observing SLAs.
- Rollback: immediate revert to previous provider route if 5xx > 1% sustained for 10 minutes.

Allowlist network hints (we'll formalize): api.redwood.com (443), address ranges + DNS names; see attached CSV template.

I'll draft the runbook and upload to the shared drive before the kickoff.

